{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Traveling Without Moving"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Advice for Travellers"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand detailed descriptions of real or imaginary events and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.<br/>Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information, including specialized articles of the professional or academic life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "region"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "area"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The traditional Tibetan culture has remained strong until now and is central to the region."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about Tibet."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grasslands "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "large flat areas with tall grass"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Huge grasslands typify the area. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "monastery"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a building where monks live and worship"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To the north, you can find numerous interesting monasteries."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "swift"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very fast"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Kham is mountainous with deep valleys where swift rivers run through. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unchanged "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "remaining as it always has been"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Here, the original Tibetan culture has survived unchanged so far."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "permit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a paper allowing you to do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Up to now, these areas have not required permits to visit."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "independent"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "without being supervised"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They haven't been allowed to travel on an independent basis. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le05ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le05ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect for Unusual Events"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense in variety of ways."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a story, you can use it to:<br/><br/>  <ul><li>refer to events that happened very recently. In these cases, you use words like <span class=\"italic\">just</span>, <span class=\"italic\">only just</span> and <span class=\"italic\">recently</span>.<br/><br/>For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Entering Tibet you feel as though <span class=\"strong\">you've just entered</span> an entirely different world</span>.<br/></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> in questions to ask about past experience or unusual events:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>notice the use of the word <span class=\"italic\">ever</span> in questions.</li> </ul> <br/>You can use words such as <span class=\"italic\">yet</span>, <span class=\"italic\">up to now</span>, <span class=\"italic\">so far</span> and <span class=\"italic\">until</span> now when you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>, since these words and phrases refer to a period of time covering the past to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Up to now</span>, these areas have not required permits to visit.<br/> The traditional Tibetan culture has remained strong <span class=\"strong\">until now</span> and is central to the region.<br/> Here, the original Tibetan culture has survived unchanged <span class=\"strong\">so far</span>. <br/> If you haven't <span class=\"strong\">yet</span>, don't. </span><br/> (You use <span class=\"italic\">yet</span> in negative statements and in questions)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You feel as though you'<span class=\"strong\">ve</span> just <span class=\"strong\">entered</span> an entirely different world."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The traditional Tibetan culture <span class=\"strong\">has remained</span> strong until now."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The original Tibetan culture <span class=\"strong\">has survived</span> unchanged so far."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Up to now, these areas <span class=\"strong\">have not required</span> permits to visit."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Tourists <span class=\"strong\">have</span> recently <span class=\"strong\">had</span> to start travelling with organised trips. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They <span class=\"strong\">haven't been</span> allowed to travel on an independent basis. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have</span> you ever <span class=\"strong\">thought</span> of trying to go off on your own? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'<span class=\"strong\">ve</span> only just <span class=\"strong\">returned</span>."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Skimming and Scanning a Text"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Skimming and scanning are two very different strategies for reading texts quickly and for getting the information you need from them without wasting time.<br/>Knowing when to use these skills will help with your reading abilities and comprehension skills."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Skimming</span>:<br/><br/> Skimming refers to looking only for the <span class=\"strong\">general or main ideas</span> in a text.<br/><br/> When you skim, your overall understanding is reduced because <span class=\"strong\">you don't read everything</span>. You read only what is important to your purpose. <br/><br/> One technique for effective skimming is <span class=\"strong\">reading only the first line of each paragraph</span>, since these are the topic sentences which will give you some clues about what the main idea of each paragraph is."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Scanning</span>:<br/><br/>  Scanning refers to looking for <span class=\"strong\">specific information</span> in a text. Examples of scanning in daily life are: bus schedules, movie schedules, phone lists, etc. When you use these kinds of texts, you are only looking for a specific detail (a number,  a date, a name, etc.).<br/><br/>  Knowing the structure of the text you want to scan will help you do it quickly (alphabetical, numerical, categorical, chronological)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try skimming and scanning the text for the general ideas and for specifics."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Entering Tibet you feel as though you've just entered an entirely different world."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Northern Tibet, or Amdo is home to the nomadic people. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Eastern Tibet, or Kham is mountainous with deep valleys."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Eating in Tibet can be monotonous. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "The Tibet experience is still worth dealing with the permits and restrictions. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library to find out about Tibetan food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down 5 or 6 different dishes and what they are made of."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the pictures and ingredients think about whether you would find the food appetising or not."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes explaining why you feel this way."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take your notes on the dishes to class and talk about them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Say what you think of this type of food and ask for others' opinions."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I go online or to the library to find out about Tibetan food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write down 5 or 6 different dishes and what they are made of."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write notes explaining why I feel the food is or is not appetising."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take my notes to class and talk about the food."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask others' opinions on it."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le05ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le05ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le05ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Entering Tibet, you feel as though you've just entered an entirely different world. The traditional Tibetan culture has remained strong until now and is central to the region.<br/>Northern Tibet, or Amdo is home to the nomadic people. Huge grasslands typify the area. It also maintains a rich culture.  To the north, you can find numerous interesting monasteries. Eastern Tibet, or Kham is mountainous with deep valleys where swift rivers run through.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le05ob05re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Both areas are wonderful to explore. Here, the original Tibetan culture has survived unchanged so far, unlike the culture in the big cities of modern Tibet. Up to now, these areas have not required permits to visit.<br/>Tourism in Tibet is now strictly controlled by the Chinese government. This means that tourists have recently had to start travelling with organised trips. They haven't been allowed to travel on an independent basis. Have you thought of trying to go off on your own? If you haven't yet, don't. There are checkpoints everywhere. You may even be stopped or questioned by the Chinese police.", "id": 2, "time": "32000", "image": "engenn10le05ob05re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Eating in Tibet can be monotonous. The diet is largely limited to barley with mutton or yak and dairy products. There are  few spices or vegetables, except for a brutally hot chili sauce often served on the side. Stop in a Chinese restaurant for an excellent wider variety of food.<br/>The Tibet experience is still worth dealing with the permits and restrictions. I've only just returned and would not have missed any of it for the world!", "id": 3, "time": "74000", "image": "engenn10le05ob05re2img03.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 2, "type": "text", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "Entering Tibet you feel as though you've just entered an entirely different world. The traditional Tibetan culture has remained strong until now and is central to the region.\n<BR/><BR/>\nNorthern Tibet, or Amdo is home to the nomadic people. Huge grasslands typify the area. It also maintains a rich culture.  To the north, you can find numerous interesting monasteries. Eastern Tibet, or Kham is mountainous with deep valleys where swift rivers run through. \n<BR/><BR/>\nBoth areas are wonderful to explore. Here, the original Tibetan culture has survived unchanged so far, unlike the culture in the big cities of modern Tibet. Up to now, these areas have not required permits to visit.\n<BR/><BR/>\n\nTourism in Tibet is now strictly controlled by the Chinese government. This means that tourists have recently had to start travelling with organised trips. They haven't been allowed to travel on an independent basis. Have you thought of trying to go off on your own? If you haven't yet, don't. There are checkpoints everywhere. You may even be stopped or questioned by the Chinese police. \n<BR/><BR/>\nEating in Tibet can be monotonous. The diet is largely limited to barley with mutton or yak and dairy products. There are  few spices or vegetables, except for a brutally hot chili sauce often served on the side. Stop in a Chinese restaurant for an excellent wider variety of food.\n<BR/><BR/>\nThe Tibet experience is still worth dealing with the permits and restrictions. I've only just returned and would not have missed any of it for the world!\n"}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about different cultures and civilizations."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about unusual events in the past. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can skim and scan a text for important information."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you know about Tibetan culture?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think people need to achieve a state of inner peace?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}]}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": " Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": " Let's travel to Tibet!"}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}]}], "stimuli_ids": [1], "id": 1, "type": "STI", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Eating in Tibet can be <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">monotonous</span>. "}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}]}, {"type": "tips", "content": [{"tip_id": 0, "type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">\u201cMonotonous\u201d </span>means boring because it does not change."}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio."}]}], "template_override": 1}, {"questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "que